- role: user
  content: |
    Let's start with a MVP for fast implementation. So, no tablet support; no multi-group assignment; no option to delete historical data; admins can create other admins; deletion of accounts instead of deactivation; no group-level export.
  timestamp: '2025-10-11T14:15:37Z'
  log_uri: 'codex-cli:2025/10/10/rollout-2025-10-10T14-55-08-0199cce6-e71f-79d1-9182-3ffefd240aa2.jsonl'
- role: assistant
  content: |
    I merged the requirements into an MVP-focused spec and applied your constraints.

    What changed
    - Deployment: Added intranet deployment and supported desktop browsers. No tablet support.
    - Auth: Kept forced owner password rotation; admins can create other admins; use account deletion (no deactivation); owner cannot be deleted.
    - Live monitoring: Added chart tooltips, current/threshold value display, device list indicators, and optional color regions.
    - History: Added zoom and threshold markers on historical charts; CSV export remains per-device only.
    - Device config: Included Modbus connection parameters; deleting a device does not delete historical readings.
    - Grouping: Each device belongs to at most one group; no group-level export.
    - Protocols: Modbus TCP required; RTU optional.
    - MVP exclusions: Explicit list at the end.

    File updated
    - specs/user/requirements.md:1

    Commit
    - 7-docs(requirements): merge Codex+Claude MVP baseline

    Next
    - Want me to open a PR from codex-requirements-iteration to codex or main, or iterate further on any section before you start composing the final single version?
